:\n                        break\n            if current_sum != count:\n                possible = False\n                break\n            # Mark these as used\n            for i in temp_used:\n                used[i] = True\n        \n        # Check if all terms are used\n        if possible:\n            total_used = sum(1 for u in used if u)\n            if total_used != len(indexed_terms):\n                possible = False\n        \n        print(\"YES\" if possible else \"NO\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n### Explanation\n1. **Fibonacci Check**: We precompute Fibonacci numbers up to a large value to check if the sum of counts plus one is a Fibonacci number.\n2. **Generate Terms**: For valid sums, generate the Fibonacci sequence terms that the string's block lengths must form.\n3. **Max Count Check**: Ensure the largest character count can accommodate the largest Fibonacci term.\n4. **Greedy Matching**: Sort counts and terms in descending order, then greedily assign terms to counts ensuring no consecutive terms are used. This ensures we can form the required block lengths while adhering to the non-consecutive term constraint.", "ground_truth_solution": null, "domain": "code", "source": "taco", "test_cases": "{\"inputs\": [\"6\\n1\\n1\\n2\\n1 1\\n2\\n1 2\\n3\\n3 1 3\\n2\\n7 5\\n6\\n26 8 3 4 13 34\\n\"], \"outputs\": [\"YES\\nYES\\nNO\\nYES\\nNO\\nYES\\n\"]}", "starter_code": ""}, {"problem": "The doctor prescribed Chef to take a multivitamin tablet 3 times a day for the next X days.\n \nChef already has Y multivitamin tablets.\n\nDetermine if Chef has enough tablets for these X days or not.\n\n------ Input Format ------ \n\n- The first line contains a single integer T \u2014 the number of test cases. Then the test cases follow.\n- The first and only line of each test case contains two space-separated integers X and Y \u2014 the number of days Chef needs to take tablets and the number of tablets Chef already has.\n\n------ Output Format